  "comments": "<span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">Chief Calarcá</span> was a native American leader and war chief. This indigenous chief was the leader of the <span style=\"font-style:italic;\">Pijaos Tribe</span>, who lived in the actual Calarcá (municipality in the eastern part of the department of Quindío, Colombia). According to the legends, Chief Calarcá died in a fight with Baltazar Maldonado, an indigenous converted into the Catholicism, to keep the power of the territory, in a fight placed on Peñas Blancas, a characteristic mountain of the actual city of Calarcá.",
